# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two jobs here:
#   1. Speed/size  - keep the 46MB OSM cache, the venv and the DB volumes out of
#                    the context that gets shipped to the Docker daemon.
#   2. Secrets     - .env and src/secrets/ must never enter an image layer.
#                    Excluding them here is stronger than deleting them in a
#                    later RUN: a deleted file still exists in the earlier layer.
#
# Both are supplied at runtime instead - see the `backend` service in
# docker-compose.yaml (env vars + a read-only bind mount for the Firebase JSON).

# ── Secrets (never bake these in) ────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
src/secrets/
secrets/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Runtime data & caches (bind-mounted at runtime, not baked) ───────────────
postgres-data/
redis-data/
cache/
map_cache/
logs/
*.log

# ── Frontend (has its own build context; node_modules never ships) ───────────
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# ── Repo/tooling noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Docs & local dev helpers not needed by the app ───────────────────────────
documentation/
deploy/
tests/
README.md
start.sh
start.ps1
test.py
my_database_erd
my_database_erd.svg
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yaml
docker-compose.*.yml
